[2026-03-15T09:41:20.111Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01SDvuoiMwFgvorUTqG5qLD2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BE8g1vMqJn2Zwy9tKZae1T","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/repo/skills/scripts/netlify-env.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":565,"cache_read_input_tokens":17151,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":565,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017x1AekfXbpQfSoyfWaKMnc","session_id":"8a9ec40f-eca3-4106-a3d3-0a22e546d865","uuid":"6af57ffe-0128-4646-8169-1ec9d0397f7b"}
[2026-03-15T09:41:20.119Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BE8g1vMqJn2Zwy9tKZae1T","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# netlify-env\n     2→\n     3→## Purpose\n     4→\n     5→Sets environment variables on a Netlify site. The Netlify CLI (`npx netlify env:set`) frequently\n     6→fails with \"No project id found\" errors in monorepo and CI environments. Use the Netlify REST API\n     7→instead.\n     8→\n     9→## Usage\n    10→\n    11→Use `curl` to call the Netlify API directly. This is more reliable than the CLI.\n    12→\n    13→### Set an environment variable\n    14→\n    15→```bash\n    16→curl -s -X POST \"https://api.netlify.com/api/v1/accounts/${NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG}/env?site_id=${NETLIFY_SITE_ID}\" \\\n    17→  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN\" \\\n    18→  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n    19→  -d '[{\"key\":\"DATABASE_URL\",\"values\":[{\"value\":\"'\"$DATABASE_URL\"'\",\"context\":\"all\"}]}]'\n    20→```\n    21→\n    22→### Update an existing environment variable\n    23→\n    24→```bash\n    25→curl -s -X PATCH \"https://api.netlify.com/api/v1/accounts/${NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG}/env/DATABASE_URL?site_id=${NETLIFY_SITE_ID}\" \\\n    26→  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN\" \\\n    27→  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n    28→  -d '{\"value\":\"'\"$DATABASE_URL\"'\",\"context\":\"all\"}'\n    29→```\n    30→\n    31→## Required Environment Variables\n    32→\n    33→- `NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN`: API authentication token.\n    34→- `NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG`: The Netlify account slug (used in the API path).\n    35→- `NETLIFY_SITE_ID`: The site to set the variable on (passed as query parameter).\n    36→\n    37→### Verify an environment variable\n    38→\n    39→```bash\n    40→curl -s \"https://api.netlify.com/api/v1/accounts/${NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG}/env/DATABASE_URL?site_id=${NETLIFY_SITE_ID}\" \\\n    41→  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN\"\n    42→```\n    43→\n    44→### Canonical workflow\n    45→\n    46→1. Read the value from `.env` (or `deployment.txt`).\n    47→2. Set via `curl -X POST` (for new variables) or `curl -X PATCH` (for existing ones).\n    48→3. Verify via `curl -X GET` to confirm the value was set correctly.\n    49→\n    50→Always use POST for initial creation. Using PATCH on a non-existent variable returns an error.\n    51→\n    52→## Notes\n    53→\n    54→- Do NOT use `npx netlify env:set` or `npx netlify env:get` — these commands fail in contexts\n    55→  where the CLI cannot resolve the project ID (monorepos, missing `.netlify/state.json`).\n    56→- The POST endpoint creates a new variable. If the variable already exists, use PATCH to update it.\n    57→- The `context` field controls which deploy contexts see the variable. Use `\"all\"` for production\n    58→  and preview deploys.\n    59→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017x1AekfXbpQfSoyfWaKMnc","session_id":"8a9ec40f-eca3-4106-a3d3-0a22e546d865","uuid":"adb847ab-a056-40fc-add8-34771545285f"}
[2026-03-15T09:41:20.125Z] {"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"ab9225d64e42441e1","tool_use_id":"toolu_017x1AekfXbpQfSoyfWaKMnc","description":"Reading skills/scripts/deploy-verification.md","usage":{"total_tokens":17765,"tool_uses":10,"duration_ms":5167},"last_tool_name":"Read","uuid":"9e9525f9-9e48-431d-9ad0-3985e1b625f2","session_id":"8a9ec40f-eca3-4106-a3d3-0a22e546d865"}
[2026-03-15T09:41:20.125Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01SDvuoiMwFgvorUTqG5qLD2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0195u5P3FaadG4QjdMzkf2e2","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/repo/skills/scripts/deploy-verification.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":565,"cache_read_input_tokens":17151,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":565,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017x1AekfXbpQfSoyfWaKMnc","session_id":"8a9ec40f-eca3-4106-a3d3-0a22e546d865","uuid":"62e84a09-e4d8-4f3a-81c0-f6700437fa1c"}
[2026-03-15T09:41:20.136Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0195u5P3FaadG4QjdMzkf2e2","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# deploy-verification\n     2→\n     3→## Purpose\n     4→\n     5→Verifies that a deployed app is fully operational after `npm run deploy` completes. Deployment\n     6→alone does not guarantee the app works — the database connection must be configured on Netlify\n     7→and API endpoints must be reachable.\n     8→\n     9→## Post-Deploy Verification Steps\n    10→\n    11→Run these steps in order after a successful `npm run deploy`:\n    12→\n    13→### 1. Set DATABASE_URL on Netlify\n    14→\n    15→The deploy script sets up the database and deploys the app, but does NOT automatically configure\n    16→the `DATABASE_URL` environment variable on the Netlify site. Without it, all backend functions\n    17→will return 500 errors.\n    18→\n    19→Set it using the Netlify REST API (see `skills/scripts/netlify-env.md`):\n    20→\n    21→```bash\n    22→curl -s -X POST \"https://api.netlify.com/api/v1/accounts/${NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG}/env?site_id=${NETLIFY_SITE_ID}\" \\\n    23→  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN\" \\\n    24→  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n    25→  -d '[{\"key\":\"DATABASE_URL\",\"values\":[{\"value\":\"'\"$DATABASE_URL\"'\",\"context\":\"all\"}]}]'\n    26→```\n    27→\n    28→### 2. Verify API endpoints return 200\n    29→\n    30→Test at least one backend endpoint to confirm the database connection works. Freshly deployed\n    31→Netlify Functions may return 502 during cold start (propagation delay). Use a retry loop\n    32→instead of failing immediately on the first attempt:\n    33→\n    34→```bash\n    35→for i in 1 2 3; do\n    36→  STATUS=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" https://<site-url>/.netlify/functions/<function-name>)\n    37→  [ \"$STATUS\" = \"200\" ] && echo \"API healthy\" && break\n    38→  echo \"Attempt $i: got $STATUS, retrying in 3s...\"\n    39→  sleep 3\n    40→done\n    41→```\n    42→\n    43→If all 3 attempts return 500, the `DATABASE_URL` is likely not set or is incorrect. If all\n    44→return 502, the function may still be propagating — wait 10–15 seconds and retry. Do not\n    45→proceed to deployment tests until API endpoints respond successfully.\n    46→\n    47→### 3. Run deployment tests\n    48→\n    49→Only run deployment tests after confirming API endpoints are healthy. Deployment tests that\n    50→hit broken endpoints will produce misleading failures.\n    51→\n    52→**Testing constraints:**\n    53→\n    54→- **No significant side effects**: Deployment tests must not perform actions with significant\n    55→  side effects (e.g., sending emails, triggering external webhooks, deleting critical data).\n    56→  Test read-heavy flows and minor CRUD operations only.\n    57→- **Revert database changes**: Any database changes made during deployment tests (created rows,\n    58→  updated records, etc.) must be reverted after the test finishes. The production database\n    59→  should be left in the same state it was in before testing. Use API DELETE endpoints or direct\n    60→  SQL cleanup to undo changes.\n    61→\n    62→## Common Failures\n    63→\n    64→- **500 from API endpoints**: `DATABASE_URL` not set on Netlify. Set it per step 1.\n    65→- **\"No project id found\" from Netlify CLI**: Use the REST API instead of `npx netlify env:set`.\n    66→  See `skills/scripts/netlify-env.md`.\n    67→- **Deployment tests fail on empty data**: If tests expect seeded data but the production database\n    68→  is empty, seed the production database or adjust tests to handle empty states.\n    69→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017x1AekfXbpQfSoyfWaKMnc","session_id":"8a9ec40f-eca3-4106-a3d3-0a22e546d865","uuid":"2c2d3e3a-a324-4a60-bcd1-a613008ba53d"}
