[2026-03-15T09:41:36.325Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01684eeGXzUSpRnvpebwb1LX","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# deploy-verification\n     2→\n     3→## Purpose\n     4→\n     5→Verifies that a deployed app is fully operational after `npm run deploy` completes. Deployment\n     6→alone does not guarantee the app works — the database connection must be configured on Netlify\n     7→and API endpoints must be reachable.\n     8→\n     9→## Post-Deploy Verification Steps\n    10→\n    11→Run these steps in order after a successful `npm run deploy`:\n    12→\n    13→### 1. Set DATABASE_URL on Netlify\n    14→\n    15→The deploy script sets up the database and deploys the app, but does NOT automatically configure\n    16→the `DATABASE_URL` environment variable on the Netlify site. Without it, all backend functions\n    17→will return 500 errors.\n    18→\n    19→Set it using the Netlify REST API (see `skills/scripts/netlify-env.md`):\n    20→\n    21→```bash\n    22→curl -s -X POST \"https://api.netlify.com/api/v1/accounts/${NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG}/env?site_id=${NETLIFY_SITE_ID}\" \\\n    23→  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN\" \\\n    24→  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n    25→  -d '[{\"key\":\"DATABASE_URL\",\"values\":[{\"value\":\"'\"$DATABASE_URL\"'\",\"context\":\"all\"}]}]'\n    26→```\n    27→\n    28→### 2. Verify API endpoints return 200\n    29→\n    30→Test at least one backend endpoint to confirm the database connection works. Freshly deployed\n    31→Netlify Functions may return 502 during cold start (propagation delay). Use a retry loop\n    32→instead of failing immediately on the first attempt:\n    33→\n    34→```bash\n    35→for i in 1 2 3; do\n    36→  STATUS=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" https://<site-url>/.netlify/functions/<function-name>)\n    37→  [ \"$STATUS\" = \"200\" ] && echo \"API healthy\" && break\n    38→  echo \"Attempt $i: got $STATUS, retrying in 3s...\"\n    39→  sleep 3\n    40→done\n    41→```\n    42→\n    43→If all 3 attempts return 500, the `DATABASE_URL` is likely not set or is incorrect. If all\n    44→return 502, the function may still be propagating — wait 10–15 seconds and retry. Do not\n    45→proceed to deployment tests until API endpoints respond successfully.\n    46→\n    47→### 3. Run deployment tests\n    48→\n    49→Only run deployment tests after confirming API endpoints are healthy. Deployment tests that\n    50→hit broken endpoints will produce misleading failures.\n    51→\n    52→**Testing constraints:**\n    53→\n    54→- **No significant side effects**: Deployment tests must not perform actions with significant\n    55→  side effects (e.g., sending emails, triggering external webhooks, deleting critical data).\n    56→  Test read-heavy flows and minor CRUD operations only.\n    57→- **Revert database changes**: Any database changes made during deployment tests (created rows,\n    58→  updated records, etc.) must be reverted after the test finishes. The production database\n    59→  should be left in the same state it was in before testing. Use API DELETE endpoints or direct\n    60→  SQL cleanup to undo changes.\n    61→\n    62→## Common Failures\n    63→\n    64→- **500 from API endpoints**: `DATABASE_URL` not set on Netlify. Set it per step 1.\n    65→- **\"No project id found\" from Netlify CLI**: Use the REST API instead of `npx netlify env:set`.\n    66→  See `skills/scripts/netlify-env.md`.\n    67→- **Deployment tests fail on empty data**: If tests expect seeded data but the production database\n    68→  is empty, seed the production database or adjust tests to handle empty states.\n    69→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a9ec40f-eca3-4106-a3d3-0a22e546d865","uuid":"9c562ef8-1576-458c-bb62-7cddf499d057","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/repo/skills/scripts/deploy-verification.md","content":"# deploy-verification\n\n## Purpose\n\nVerifies that a deployed app is fully operational after `npm run deploy` completes. Deployment\nalone does not guarantee the app works — the database connection must be configured on Netlify\nand API endpoints must be reachable.\n\n## Post-Deploy Verification Steps\n\nRun these steps in order after a successful `npm run deploy`:\n\n### 1. Set DATABASE_URL on Netlify\n\nThe deploy script sets up the database and deploys the app, but does NOT automatically configure\nthe `DATABASE_URL` environment variable on the Netlify site. Without it, all backend functions\nwill return 500 errors.\n\nSet it using the Netlify REST API (see `skills/scripts/netlify-env.md`):\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://api.netlify.com/api/v1/accounts/${NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG}/env?site_id=${NETLIFY_SITE_ID}\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '[{\"key\":\"DATABASE_URL\",\"values\":[{\"value\":\"'\"$DATABASE_URL\"'\",\"context\":\"all\"}]}]'\n```\n\n### 2. Verify API endpoints return 200\n\nTest at least one backend endpoint to confirm the database connection works. Freshly deployed\nNetlify Functions may return 502 during cold start (propagation delay). Use a retry loop\ninstead of failing immediately on the first attempt:\n\n```bash\nfor i in 1 2 3; do\n  STATUS=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" https://<site-url>/.netlify/functions/<function-name>)\n  [ \"$STATUS\" = \"200\" ] && echo \"API healthy\" && break\n  echo \"Attempt $i: got $STATUS, retrying in 3s...\"\n  sleep 3\ndone\n```\n\nIf all 3 attempts return 500, the `DATABASE_URL` is likely not set or is incorrect. If all\nreturn 502, the function may still be propagating — wait 10–15 seconds and retry. Do not\nproceed to deployment tests until API endpoints respond successfully.\n\n### 3. Run deployment tests\n\nOnly run deployment tests after confirming API endpoints are healthy. Deployment tests that\nhit broken endpoints will produce misleading failures.\n\n**Testing constraints:**\n\n- **No significant side effects**: Deployment tests must not perform actions with significant\n  side effects (e.g., sending emails, triggering external webhooks, deleting critical data).\n  Test read-heavy flows and minor CRUD operations only.\n- **Revert database changes**: Any database changes made during deployment tests (created rows,\n  updated records, etc.) must be reverted after the test finishes. The production database\n  should be left in the same state it was in before testing. Use API DELETE endpoints or direct\n  SQL cleanup to undo changes.\n\n## Common Failures\n\n- **500 from API endpoints**: `DATABASE_URL` not set on Netlify. Set it per step 1.\n- **\"No project id found\" from Netlify CLI**: Use the REST API instead of `npx netlify env:set`.\n  See `skills/scripts/netlify-env.md`.\n- **Deployment tests fail on empty data**: If tests expect seeded data but the production database\n  is empty, seed the production database or adjust tests to handle empty states.\n","numLines":69,"startLine":1,"totalLines":69}}}
